=== the claim under test: spread ACROSS sensors at fixed noise ===
  kappa_g varies 100x between 'aligned' and 'mix f=0.01'.  If the
  readout is kappa_g-invariant, the spread must sit far below the
  common bias, which is an extraction artefact shared by all.
  noise  | alpha spread | slope spread | common bias (alpha, slope)
  0e+00 |       1.818% |      11.649% | +1.61%, +13.95%
  1e-04 |       1.813% |      11.646% | +1.60%, +13.90%
  1e-03 |       1.772% |      11.627% | +1.54%, +13.54%
  1e-02 |       1.364% |      11.443% | +0.94%, +9.97%

  tolerance: the readout error grows as eta/kappa_g, so a sensor with
  kappa_g a factor K below the best available needs a noise floor K
  times lower to reach the same accuracy.  The blind set is measure
  zero but its neighbourhood is not, which is the real constraint --
  and it is a signal-to-noise constraint, not a modelling one.
